%% HAND-CURATED. Coordinates with sys-09 (OTA) for FW update carrying new next_key, and sys-13 for rotation audit log.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant SecurityEngineer
    participant KMS
    participant OtaService
    participant FleetDevices
    participant ConfigService

    Note over SecurityEngineer,FleetDevices: Stage 1 — generate new key in KMS
    SecurityEngineer->>KMS: CreateKey {KeySpec=ECC_NIST_P256, KeyUsage=SIGN_VERIFY}
    KMS-->>SecurityEngineer: new_key_id

    Note over SecurityEngineer,FleetDevices: Stage 2 — ship FW update with new public key in next_key slot (sys-09)
    SecurityEngineer->>OtaService: prepare FW release embedding new_pubkey in next_key
    OtaService->>FleetDevices: staged rollout (sys-09 5%→25%→50%→100%)

    loop wait for ≥99% fleet adoption (typically weeks)
        SecurityEngineer->>OtaService: GET /admin/ota/release/:id/status
        OtaService-->>SecurityEngineer: rollout_progress_percentage
        alt fleet_adoption_below_threshold
            Note over SecurityEngineer: pause rotation — investigate stuck devices
        end
    end

    Note over SecurityEngineer,FleetDevices: Stage 3 — switch active signing key
    SecurityEngineer->>ConfigService: env var CONFIG_SIGNING_KMS_KEY_ID = new_key_id (deploy)
    ConfigService->>ConfigService: next signing uses new key
    ConfigService->>FleetDevices: subsequent configs signed with new_key (devices verify with embedded next_key, promote to current_key)

    Note over SecurityEngineer,FleetDevices: Stage 4 — decommission old key
    SecurityEngineer->>SecurityEngineer: confirm all active devices fetched ≥1 config signed by new key
    alt old_key_decommission_blocked (devices still verifying with old key)
        Note over SecurityEngineer: wait — retain old key in KMS until 100% migrated
    else success
        SecurityEngineer->>KMS: ScheduleKeyDeletion {old_key_id, pending=30 days}
        KMS-->>SecurityEngineer: deletion scheduled
    end

    Note over SecurityEngineer,ConfigService: annual ceremony · audit row in key_rotation_log (sys-13) · failure rollback per sys-13 §6 §rotation-failure-rollback
